// Squad banter: Ambient conversations, played among a player's own squad members with no window.
// Each line goes to the feed and floats over whoever says it, like a bark. A squad banters after a
// fight ends and now and then while idle - rarely, on purpose.
//
// participants names who says each line: the squad members are cast when it plays, and every line
// starts with one of those names. In requires, the first participant is the Speaker and the second
// the Listener. An Ambient conversation can't offer choices - nobody is at a window to pick one.
//
// Compile with: ysc compile banter.yarn -o . -n banter

title: SettlerBanterWater
kind: Ambient
participants: First, Second
requires: Speaker.Definition == Settler; Listener.Definition == Settler
---
First: How much water's left? #line:banter_water_ask
Second: Enough, if nobody asks again. #line:banter_water_answer
First: I'm only asking. #line:banter_water_only
Second: That's twice now. #line:banter_water_twice
===

// Wins over the water whenever the first speaker is hurt - which, after a fight, is most of the time.
title: SettlerBanterAfterFight
kind: Ambient
participants: First, Second
requires: Speaker.Definition == Settler; Listener.Definition == Settler; Speaker.Health < 0.7
priority: 5
---
First: Tell me that was the last of them. #line:banter_fight_last
Second: That was the last of them. #line:banter_fight_lie
First: You're a bad liar. #line:banter_fight_liar
===
